{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793529364,"nonce":"2xu7PvXFLwK1VOWfp1zX/7j9R5Q=","title":"An outline-color transition started by an attribute change never lands","message":"Found porting cn::number_gauge (5f0c8eb). With\n\n    .g { outline: 2px solid transparent; outline-offset: 2px;\n         transition: outline-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out); }\n    .g[data-focus-visible] { outline-color: var(--focus-ring); }\n\nand the attribute toggled in place by `Div::attr_when(\"data-focus-visible\", \"\", computed)`, the node's `props.outline_color` stays `rgba(0,0,0,0)` after `Headless::settle()`. The attribute is in the element's class list (`data-focus-visible=`). Dropping `outline-color` from the `transition` makes the rule apply at once, so matching works and the transition is what stalls.\n\nA `border-color` transition on the same element driven by `:hover` completes, so this is either outline-color specifically or transitions started from a class/attribute binding (ClassPendingBinding restyle) rather than a pointer-state restyle.\n\nWorkaround in the gauge: no outline transition; the ring snaps on. ashui eases `outline-width`.\n\nReproduce: put the transition back in `.cn-number-gauge` in CN_STYLES and run `keys_move_it_only_once_pressed` in crates/blinc_recorder/tests/cn_number_gauge_snapshots.rs, printing `props.outline_color` after `ui.key(39).settle()`.","files":null}]}